            <ArticleTitle>Derivation and characterization of the NYSCFe003-A human embryonic stem cell line.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-220</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1873-5061(17)30220-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.scr.2017.10.017</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The human embryonic stem cell line NYSCFe003-A was derived from a day 5 to day 6 blastocyst in feeder-free and antibiotic free conditions. The blastocyst was voluntarily donated for research as surplus after in vitro fertilization treatment following informed consent. The NYSCFe003-A line expresses all the pluripotency markers and has the potential to differentiate into all three germ layers in vitro. The line presents normal karyotype and is mycoplasma free.</AbstractText>
